  "derivation": "Written CR-01..CR-14 review of every success-path variant (no compiler output used; spec §11.2): neutral and grid are the vendored profiles; support as in cn-compile-support-profile, support-abort adds a refuse step (no write); grid-extraction replaces import by ai on three base fields (valid deltas, no recipe writes them); the cn variants add recipes whose every action maps to its declared writes (identical demands coalesce), whose written fields list the phase actor (code for complete/normalize, editor for commands) in the cn base, whose created types are admitted by their containment and whose ID modes agree with id admission; count uses select and reachable from/to as pinned in the schema; inverseReference properties belong to the referencing type. The compiled identity is the §5.1 record whose sha256 is H(variant profile). Wire shape (parity sync PS-35): one PureResult {status: ok, payload, diagnostics: []} per variant in input order, payload UNSEALED (CompiledProfile has no wire shape; the member must exist); the identities are sealed apart as the compiled-identities artifact, one {variant, identity} per variant.",
